[
  {
    "sha": "0e96ca1c0a0b888836d7e09ac3cca1f8425722d9",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDBlOTZjYTFjMGEwYjg4ODgzNmQ3ZTA5YWMzY2NhMWY4NDI1NzIyZDk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:27:01Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T09:27:01Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(edm): Wire Contour skim passes - per-pass condition, offset and direction\n\nA rough pass then N skims, each naming its own machine condition (its\noffset is that condition's wire radius + gap) and optionally walked\nthe other way round. Skims ride the op params (file / MCP JSON\n`skims`, absent when empty), EditOperationParams and the stamp. The\ncommand door refuses a skim naming no condition or an unstated one, a\npass nearer the profile than the finishing pass, a skim farther out\nthan the pass before it, and a skim condition for another wire - each\nby name. The generator runs the single-pass generator per pass at its\nown offset; the wire stream announces each skim with a mid-section\nPARAM EdmCondition and wire-iso.cps selects it (comp off again) with\nthe wire still threaded. Rough-only output is byte-identical to #533's\ngolden; new golden wire_contour_punch_skims.nc.\n\nFixes #538\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "a127ca5bbb4f24382df7cdd2e879e5a9784fa9f6",
